# DNA-AND content · life · intelligent creatures (any kingdom)
# researched: Cambridge comparative-cognition work on corvids and cephalopods (Schnell, Amodio, Clayton);
#   Phys.org 2020 review "Evolution of complex cognition in birds"; mirror-test literature (Gallup 1970,
#   later studies of apes, dolphins, elephants, magpies, cleaner wrasse); CARTA "Dolphin and Elephant Minds";
#   standard biology for social-insect collective behavior and slime-mold problem solving
# Any line of life can climb to intelligence (the grouping ladder). These are the real minds that seed it.
# Spec: docs/CONTENT-FORMAT.md · wiki/systems/r08-life-sim.md · wiki/systems/r09-civilization.md

# ── Real thinking animals (seeds) ──

@mind great-apes
name: Great apes
real: yes
shows: tool use, culture, self-recognition, sign-language learning in captivity, politics and war

@mind humans
name: Humans
real: yes
shows: language, writing, technology, civilization; the only species known to reach space

@mind corvids
name: Crows and ravens
real: yes
shows: tool making, planning ahead, solving puzzles, recognizing faces; minds that evolved separately from apes'

@mind parrots
name: Parrots
real: yes
shows: speech, counting, problem solving

@mind dolphins-whales
name: Dolphins and whales
real: yes
shows: self-recognition, names (signature whistles), culture passed between groups, songs

@mind elephants
name: Elephants
real: yes
shows: self-recognition, mourning their dead, long memory, family culture

@mind octopuses
name: Octopuses
real: yes
shows: problem solving, escape, camouflage; a smart line with no social life and short lives

@mind wolves-dogs
name: Wolves and dogs
real: yes
shows: pack hunting strategy, reading faces and gestures

@mind magpies
name: Magpies
real: yes
shows: one of the few birds reported to pass the mirror test

@mind cleaner-wrasse
name: Cleaner wrasse
real: yes
shows: a small fish reported to pass the mirror test

@mind social-insects
name: Social insects
real: yes
shows: no single smart brain, but colonies that solve problems together: farming, building, war, voting on new nests

@mind slime-mold
name: Slime molds
real: yes
shows: with no brain at all, they solve mazes and find the shortest paths

# ── Signs of a mind ──

@sign tool-use
name: Tool use
real: yes

@sign tool-making
name: Tool making
real: yes

@sign self-recognition
name: Self-recognition
real: yes
says: knowing yourself in a mirror; one test of a mind

@sign planning
name: Planning ahead
real: yes

@sign language
name: Language
real: yes

@sign culture
name: Culture
real: yes
says: ways of doing things taught, not born with

@sign mourning
name: Mourning
real: yes

@sign deception
name: Deception
real: yes

@sign teaching
name: Teaching
real: yes

@sign collective-mind
name: Collective mind
real: yes
says: many small minds acting as one (hives, swarms)

# ── What pushes a line toward intelligence ──

@driver social-life
name: Living in groups
real: yes
says: tracking friends, rivals and debts takes a bigger brain

@driver hands
name: Grasping limbs
real: yes
says: hands, trunks, beaks, tentacles that can handle tools

@driver long-life
name: Long life and long childhood
real: yes
says: more time to learn and to teach

@driver varied-food
name: Hard-to-get food
real: yes
says: nuts, shellfish, prey that must be outwitted

@driver brain-size
name: Big brain for its body
real: yes
says: brain size compared to body size is one rough sign, but not the only one

@driver changing-world
name: A changing world
real: yes
says: fast-changing climates reward clever, flexible animals

@driver convergence
name: Many roads to a mind
real: yes
says: crows, apes and octopuses reached cleverness separately; minds evolve again and again

# ── Generator rules ──

@rule mind-any-line
real: rule
says: any kingdom can reach intelligence if evolution builds the drivers: animals most often, but hive insects, fungal networks and even plants on other templates can climb the grouping ladder

@rule mind-signs-ladder
real: rule
says: a species earns signs of a mind one by one (tool use, culture, language…); together they unlock the thinking steps (31+) on the grouping ladder

@rule mind-own-image
real: rule
says: a thinking species' clothing, tools, cities and ships are generated from its own body plan (LAW 14)

@rule mind-ai-layers
real: rule
says: thinking species get the species AI layer, and can later grow a galactic mind

@rule mind-spark
real: rule
says: the Spark of Mind power pushes a species toward intelligence, but only works on one already close to it
